For mpv 0.42.0. Not from upstream.

After a seek, restart the video at once and let the audio join it in sync.

Audio handed to the audio output is heard one output latency later: 13 ms
on a MacBook's speakers, 171 ms on AirPods Pro. mpv restarts the audio at
the pts of the first video frame after the seek, and it times every later
frame against the audio that is being heard. So the second frame waits
until the audio of the first has come out, and the picture stands still for
the latency after every seek.

With this patch the audio restarts at the pts the video will have reached
when it is first heard, so the audio that would have played during the
latency is left out. The sound comes back at the same moment as before.
The picture no longer waits for it.

  audio/out/buffer.c   Remembers the latency of a pull AO from each read by
                       the device (ao_get_latency), and has ao_get_delay()
                       include it from the moment playback starts and not
                       only from the device's first read after it.
  player/audio.c       On a seek with video, moves the audio start pts by
                       the latency and tells the A/V sync so (mpctx->delay).

Only seeks with video are changed, and only on pull AOs (CoreAudio is one)
whose device has read from mpv before, which is how the latency is known.
A file that starts at a position starts with a seek, so this applies to it
when the audio output is still open from the file before. Pausing and
unpausing during playback and audio-only playback are not changed.

